 ```
 
+### Parallel execution with communication
+
+Enable communication with `communication: true` and optionally assign each task a stable `id`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "communication": true,
+  "tasks": [
+    { "id": "api", "agent": "worker", "task": "Trace the public API and tell tests about constraints." },
+    { "id": "tests", "agent": "worker", "task": "Design regression tests and tell api about edge cases." }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Worker IDs must be unique within the dispatch. If omitted, they default to `worker-1`, `worker-2`, and so on, so repeated uses of the same agent definition remain independently addressable.
+
+Communication adds these tools to every worker:
+
+| Tool | Arguments | Result |
+|------|-----------|--------|
+| `team_list` | `{}` | This worker and all teammates with agent names and current status |
+| `team_send` | `{ recipient, message }` | Delivery acceptance for one running teammate, or an explicit error |
+| `team_broadcast` | `{ message }` | Accepted worker IDs plus every failed recipient and reason |
+
+Example worker calls:
+
+```json
+{ "recipient": "tests", "message": "The parser rejects empty names; cover that case." }
+```
+
+```json
+{ "message": "The shared interface requires UTF-8 byte lengths, not JavaScript string lengths." }
+```
+
+Incoming messages are inserted automatically before the recipient's next model call with the sender's worker ID, agent name, and complete text. Delivery waits for the current response and its tool calls; it does not interrupt a running tool. A worker cannot finish while an already accepted message is still pending. Sending confirms acceptance only and does not wait for the recipient to reply.
+
+Messages are private to one parallel dispatch. The parent creates an authenticated loopback broker for that dispatch and closes it when the dispatch completes or is cancelled. Only running teammates can receive messages, the sender is excluded from broadcasts, and each message may contain at most 256 KiB of UTF-8 data.
+
